  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training and Dissemination of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) among selected Diocesan Carit</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 2030 Agenda constitutes 17 new Sustainable Development Goals (applicable to all countries) which promote peaceful and inclusive societies, create better jobs and tackle environment challenges, particularly climate change. The DRC government agrees with the SDGs and the government&#x2019;s policies and funding environment will be guided by these goals for the next 15 years. Consequently Caritas Congo has aligned their goals to these global goals and has taken the lead to train all their Diocesan Caritas on the SDGs so as to be better positioned for future funding opportunity. With this particular project Caritas Congo will train an additional 4 dioceses on SDGs and will engage with the CODD alliance to disseminate and advocate with the government over the SDGs and how they can be translated into practice in the DRC context.</narrative>
  </description>
